  "id": "orienting-response",
  "term": "orienting response",
  "definition": "An orienting response is an automatic attention-and-body reaction to a significant event, reflected here by autonomic changes such as pupil dilation. In this context, it is described as a response triggered by an error that can influence how behavior is adjusted on the next trial.",
